# Acting overgroups of the paired symplectic module

The extension modules provide actual binary intertwining maps from arbitrary
diagram-moving twists to the canonical graph pair, the literal binary
normalizer and a concrete candidate generated overgroup, and fixed-space
obstructions for swapping and coefficient-field involutions.

Normalizer coverage, its elementary two-subgroup geometry, and the resulting
unconditional acting-overgroup parameter bounds remain separate obligations.
These reductions do not claim the completed H.7 parameter calculation.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith H.7, printed pp.388–389 of `refs/quasithin.pdf`.
-/
